# Recorded device sessions are NEVER committed, and unlike the BVH corpus's
# fetched half there is no upstream to pull them from either: a mocopi session
# is a real person's motion, and a skeleton packet is a body measurement of that
# person. What survives is manifest.json beside this file — the hashes and the
# measurements — which is what the corpus splits on: redistribution, never worth
# (docs/roadmap/adapters-mocopi-vmc-ardy.md §9.2).
#
# Everything, not a list of extensions. What could land here is a capture, a
# trace exported from one, a clip baked from that, or an analysis dump — and an
# extension list fails open, on exactly the bytes that must not be committed.
# manifest.json is the one file this directory carries, so it is the one
# exception.
*
!.gitignore
!manifest.json
